hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19302","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Shubah informed us from Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik from Usayd ibn Hudayr, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, he said: A man from the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not employ me as you employed so-and-so? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You will meet after me exclusive selfishness, so be patient until you meet me tomorrow at the Hawd."
"19303","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah from Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Amr from his mother Fatimah the daughter of Husayn from Aishah, that she used to say: Usayd ibn Hudayr was among the most excellent of people, and he used to say: If only I could remain as I am in three states among my states: when I recite the Quran, and when I hear it recited, and when I hear the sermon of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and when I witness a funeral; and I never witnessed a funeral at all but that I spoke to myself of nothing but what will be done with it and what it will come to."
"19304","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik from Usayd ibn Hudayr, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, he said: A man from the Ansar drew aside with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Will you not employ me as you employed so-and-so? He said: You will meet after me exclusive selfishness, so be patient until you meet me at the Hawd."
"19305","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us from his father from his grandfather Alqamah from Aishah, she said: We arrived from a Hajj or an Umrah, and we were met at Dhu al-Hulayfah, and young servants from the Ansar had gone out to meet their families, and they met Usayd ibn Hudayr and announced to him the death of his wife, so he covered his face and began to weep. She said: So I said to him: May Allah forgive you, you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and you have the precedence and seniority that you have; why do you weep over a woman? So he uncovered his head and said: You speak truly; by my life, I have a right not to weep over anyone after Sad ibn Muadh, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said concerning him what he said. She said: I said to him: What did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say concerning him? He said: The Throne shook for the death of Sad ibn Muadh. She said: And he was walking between me and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"19306","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us from Abdillah ibn Abdillah from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Usayd ibn Hudayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Perform ablution from camel meat, and do not perform ablution from sheep meat, and pray in the resting places of sheep, and do not pray in the kneeling places of camels."
"19307","Muhammad ibn Muqatil al-Marwazi narrated to us: Abbad ibn al-Awwam informed us: al-Hajjaj narrated to us from Abdillah ibn Abdillah, the freedman of Banu Hashim, he said, and he was trustworthy, he said, and al-Hakam used to take from him, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Usayd ibn Hudayr from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he was asked about camel milk, he said: Perform ablution from its milk; and he was asked about sheep milk, and he said: Do not perform ablution from its milk."
